.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-AGENT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-agent
.Nd the interface an automated actor uses to this machine
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm describe Op Fl -text
.Nm
.Cm capabilities | audit Oo Fl n Ar count Oc
.Nm
.Cm do | send Ar verb Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
answers what this machine is, and changes it within a list somebody
declared.
.Bl -tag -width "describe --text"
.It Cm describe
One JSON document: hardware, firmware, block devices, network, state,
drift, health, packages, idle, sandboxed programs and, on an A/B
machine, the root slots.
.It Cm describe Fl -text
The same document as a table.
It is a
.Em view
of the JSON rather than a second answer: each gatherer reads its
sources once and branches only at the point of printing.
.It Cm capabilities
Whether
.Cm do
is enabled, and which verbs are permitted.
.It Cm audit Op Fl n Ar count
What has been attempted, refusals included.
.It Cm do Ar verb Op Ar argument ...
Change the machine.
.It Cm send Ar verb Op Ar argument ...
The same, over
.Nm novi-agentd Ns 's
socket, for a caller who is not root but is in the
.Sy agent
group.
.El
.Ss Reading is free, writing is declared
.Cm describe ,
.Cm capabilities
and
.Cm audit
are a formatted view of files any user can already read, so they need
no permission and grant none.
.Pp
.Cm do
needs
.Em two
keys in
.Xr system.conf 5 :
.Va agent.enabled = on
and the verb named in
.Va agent.allow .
One key would mean a machine that grants powers because a program was
installed, which is a service registry with a policy file attached.
.Ss Verbs
.Bl -tag -width "state.rollback [gen]" -compact
.It Cm state.set Ar key Ar value
Declare a value.
Does not apply it.
.It Cm state.apply
Converge the machine to the document.
.It Cm state.rollback Op Ar generation
Restore a previous generation and re-apply.
.It Cm pkg.sync
Refresh the signed package index.
.It Cm pkg.install Ar name ...
Install packages.
.It Cm wifi.join Ar ssid
Join a network.
The passphrase is read from standard input and never appears in
.Ar argv ,
so the verb is not available over
.Cm send :
a one-line request has nowhere to put a secret.
.El
.Pp
There is deliberately no
.Cm exec
verb and no
.Cm service.start .
The first is the absence of a boundary wearing a policy file; the
second is drift by construction, and an agent that produces drift on
purpose defeats the engine it is talking to.
Services are reached with
.Cm state.set
and
.Cm state.apply ,
like everything else.
.Ss The rate limit is not a security control
.Va agent.rate
bounds an
.Em accident .
Anything that can run
.Nm
can run
.Xr pkg 1
directly, so the limit stands between nobody and nothing.
What it buys is legibility: a buggy actor looping on one install
becomes a run of
.Dq rate limit
refusals in the audit log, where a thousand successes would say
nothing.
Only
.Em allowed
calls count toward it; counting refusals would make it
self-sustaining.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "NOVI_AGENT_PEER_UID" -compact
.It Ev NOVI_AGENT_VIA
Set by
.Nm novi-agent-serve
so a request that arrived over the socket is audited as such.
.It Ev NOVI_AGENT_PEER_UID
The peer's uid, from
.Dv SO_PEERCRED .
Identity comes from the kernel, never from the request.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/log/novi-agent.jsonl" -compact
.It Pa /var/log/novi-agent.jsonl
The audit log, mode 0600, one JSON object per line.
Refusals are recorded as well as successes: a boundary that records
only what it let through tells you nothing about what was tried.
.It Pa /run/novi/agent/sock
The socket, when
.Va services.novi-agentd
is on.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A refused verb exits non-zero and says which key would permit it.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Look at the machine:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ novi-agent describe --text
.Ed
.Pp
Permit two verbs and use one:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# novi-state set agent.enabled on
# novi-state set agent.allow "state.set state.apply"
# novi-state apply
# novi-agent do state.set hostname workshop
# novi-agent do state.apply
.Ed
.Pp
What has been tried, including what was refused:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# novi-agent audit -n 20
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-state 1 ,
.Xr novi-wifi 1 ,
.Xr pkg 1 ,
.Xr system.conf 5
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0029, RFC 0032.
